<h2>6. Checking the results is your job</h2>
<p>PointerPath is a design aid. It does not replace engineering judgement.</p>
<ul>
<li>The paths it draws come from a mathematical model of a vehicle and from what you give it: the vehicle, the route, the speed and settings, and the drawing and its units. Real vehicles and drivers differ.</li>
<li>The built-in vehicles are based on the design vehicles described in AS/NZS 2890.1 and AS 2890.2. PointerPath is not published, endorsed or certified by Standards Australia or any road authority. Check the vehicle dimensions against the standard or guideline that applies to your job.</li>
<li>You are responsible for checking PointerPath's output, for deciding whether it is suitable for your purpose, and for the designs and advice you produce with it.</li>
